\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. How blest is life if lived for Thee,
\par My loving Saviour and my Lord:
\par No pleasures that the world can give
\par Such perfect gladness can afford.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. To know I am Thy ransomed child,
\par Bought by Thine own most precious blood,
\par And from Thy loving hand to take
\par With grateful heart each gift of good;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. All day to walk beneath Thy smile,
\par Watching Thine eye to guide me still,
\par To rest at night beneath Thy care,
\par Guarded by Thee from every ill;
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. To feel that though I journey on
\par By stony paths and rugged ways,
\par Thy blessed feet have gone before,
\par And strength is given for weary days.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Such love shall ever make me glad,
\par Strong in Thy strength to work or rest,
\par Until I see Thee face to face,
\par And in Thy light am fully blest.
\par \f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\fs16 
\par }

